{"name":"California Sagebrush","hex":"#959988","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sagebrush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several North American aromatic shrubs of the genus Artemisia, having silvery-grey, green leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sagebrush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Artemisia californica","blocks":[{"text":"Artemisia californica, also known as California sagebrush or cowboy cologne, is a species of shrub in the sunflower family that is endemic to western California and northwestern Baja California."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/ArtemisiaCalifornica-GaviotaCA.jpg/330px-ArtemisiaCalifornica-GaviotaCA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_californica"},{"title":"California","blocks":[{"text":"California is a state in the Western United States. It is bordered by Oregon to the north, the Mexican state of Baja California to the south, Nevada to the east, Arizona to the southeast, and the Pacific Ocean to the west. With a population of over 39 million across an area of 163,696 square miles (423,970 km2), it is the most populous U.S. state and the third largest by land area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Flag_of_California.svg/330px-Flag_of_California.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/California"},{"title":"Sagebrush","blocks":[{"text":"Sagebrush is the common name of several woody and herbaceous species of plants in the genus Artemisia. The best-known sagebrush is the shrub Artemisia tridentata. Sagebrush is native to the western half of North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Sagebrushsjc.jpg/330px-Sagebrushsjc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.